{
  "dom_id": "step-q98752",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/3114d1c94b63a2506a66e701346bc7367b901659b78a2cf7c191648c96a716dc.png)\n\nConsider the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=f(y)$ where the graph of $f(y)$ is shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $y=3$ is a node.\n- $y=-1$ is a sink.\n- $y=-1$ is a source.",
  "worked_solution": "We can classify the equilibrium solutions of an autonomous ODE ${y}^{\u2032}=f(y)$ by examining its phase line.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *sink* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *toward* the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *source* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line both point *away* from the equilibrium solution.\n\n- An equilibrium solution is a *node* if the arrows directly above and below it on the phase line point in the same direction.\n\nThe phase line that corresponds to the given graph is as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14042839/assets/f72f89ecad74cc708b5950763002757d9d012d3859c7a5bd5eb19ae60fc54e55.png)\n\nTherefore, we have:\n\n- Statement I is false. From the phase line, we see that $y=3$ is a sink.\n\n- Statement II is false while statement III is true. From the phase line, we see that $y=-1$ is a source.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only\".",
